WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.402
Open courses. A full semester in every class on the first day. 12 open courses, published as signed packages a district installs into its own library.

2
00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:12.467
educateos.io/courses: 12 semester-long courses, three per grade band, published by educateos.io as signed open course packages.

3
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:20.275
educateos.io/courses: Every course's full outline is public: anyone can read it without signing in.

4
00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:26.875
educateos.io/courses: Each unit lists its activities and the standards it teaches. Teacher guides and answer keys stay out of public view.

5
00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:31.516
In the demo · Teacher Studio: In the district, Mr. Ortega's World History 7 class has the course installed as editable modules.

6
00:00:31.516 --> 00:00:37.399
In the demo · Teacher Studio: Every unit says where it came from: the package, its publisher and its version.

7
00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:43.116
In the demo · Teacher Studio: Teacher guides and answer keys arrive as teacher-only notes, which students never see.

8
00:00:43.116 --> 00:00:51.134
In the demo · Teacher Studio: Add a course previews another package first: what it would add as drafts, and that nothing already there changes.

9
00:00:51.134 --> 00:01:02.002
District office · course library: The district's course library holds each signed course, checked against its publisher's signature before it is stored.

10
00:01:02.002 --> 00:01:06.002
Browse the catalog at educateos.io/courses. Every outline is public. Teacher guides and answer keys come with each unit, for teachers only.
